    "question": {
      ":question/id": "851262bb-aa7f-5f6f-8490-f545633dafc1",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sin\\left(144^\\circ\\right)}{\\cos\\left(72^\\circ\\right)}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write $s=\\sin\\left(72^\\circ\\right)$ and $c=\\cos\\left(72^\\circ\\right)$. The **double-angle formula** gives $\\sin\\left(144^\\circ\\right)=2sc$.\n\n\n\nExpand the doubled sine and cancel the common factor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2sc}{c} &=2s \\\\ &=2\\sin\\left(72^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll cancellations use nonzero factors in the original expression.",
